@startuml
title APT-SD-D02 Terminal Mode Model: Cashier-Assisted vs Continuity Terminal
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Unassigned : terminal provisioned
Unassigned --> Assigned : device assigned to Site/Site Group
Assigned --> CashierReady : trusted device + cashier + shift
CashierReady --> CashierWorkflow : normal staffed transaction
CashierWorkflow --> CashierReady : completion / governed cancel

Assigned --> ContinuityEligible : approved continuity scope exists
ContinuityEligible --> ContinuityActive : authorized activation
ContinuityActive --> RestrictedOperation : cashier confirms incident scope
RestrictedOperation --> ContinuityActive : transaction complete / exception handoff
ContinuityActive --> RestorationReview : deactivation
RestorationReview --> CashierReady : post-restoration review complete

Assigned --> Blocked : untrusted device / invalid scope / no shift
Blocked --> Assigned : authorized correction

note right of ContinuityEligible
Continuity Terminal is disabled by default.
It is not an implicit fallback from normal failure.
end note
@enduml
